# Deny everything, then name the build inputs. A deny list would have to be
# kept in step with every new runtime file, and the cost of missing one is
# config/.env with the live provider keys, or data/cache.redb with the prompt
# history, baked into the build stage layer. `cargo build --release` needs
# these three paths and nothing else. The Dockerfile itself is always sent.
*
!src
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
